// CS383 quiz bank. k: mc = multiple choice (a = index of correct option), tf = true/false
QUIZ={id:"cs383",mids:["472","471","462","461","451"],code:"CS383",topics:{l1:"L1 Intro I",l2:"L2 Intro II · Ethics",l3:"L3 Process Models",l4:"L4 Agile &amp; Scrum",l5:"L5 Process Quality",l6:"L6 Project Mgmt",l7:"L7 Requirements",l8:"L8 Req. Engineering"},
bank:[
{id:"a1",t:"l1",k:"mc",q:"Software is:",o:["A computer program and its associated documentation", "The source code that runs on a computer", "The hardware together with its drivers", "The executable file delivered to users"],a:0,e:"البرنامج مع التوثيق حقه، مو الكود بس."},
{id:"a2",t:"l1",m:["451"],k:"tf",q:"Software development costs more than software maintenance.",a:false,e:"ميد 451. الصيانة والتطوير بعد التسليم (Maintenance and Evolution) أغلى."},
{id:"a3",t:"l1",m:["451"],k:"mc",q:"The following is an example of a generic software product:",o:["Microsoft PowerPoint","Patient registration application of a private hospital","A stock prediction application for one company","Air traffic control system"],a:0,e:"ميد 451. Generic يتباع لأي عميل في السوق، والباقي مبني لجهة وحدة (Customized)."},
{id:"a4",t:"l1",k:"mc",q:"Which is a customized software product?",o:["Air traffic control system","Microsoft Office","CAD software","A dental clinic appointment system sold on the market"],a:0,e:"Customized مبني لعميل واحد حسب طلبه، مثل air traffic control و embedded control systems."},
{id:"a5",t:"l1",m:["451"],k:"mc",q:"Motivation behind software engineering includes:",o:["To handle development and maintenance cost","To rapidly produce large software systems","To distinguish market needs of software","To remove the need for testing"],a:0,e:"ميد 451. من تحديات SE: التعامل مع تكلفة التطوير والصيانة العالية."},
{id:"a6",t:"l1",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"According to \"Application types\", what determines which engineering methods and tools to use?",o:["Application type, customer requirements, team background, and tools","Project manager's personal preference","Software cost alone","The programming language only"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. أربع أشياء: نوع التطبيق، متطلبات العميل، خلفية الفريق، والأدوات."},
{id:"a7",t:"l1",k:"mc",q:"Which issue is about blocking unauthorized people and protecting information?",o:["Security and trust","Heterogeneity","Scale","Business and social change"],a:0,e:"Security and trust."},
{id:"a8",t:"l1",k:"mc",q:"Systems that must work as distributed systems across networks with different devices relate to:",o:["Heterogeneity","Scale","Security and trust","Diversity"],a:0,e:"Heterogeneity: أجهزة وشبكات مختلفة."},
{id:"a9",t:"l1",k:"mc",q:"Compared with software engineering, system engineering is:",o:["More general: hardware, software and process","More specific: software only","The same thing","Only about testing"],a:0,e:"System engineering أعم، و Software engineering يركز على البرنامج بس."},
{id:"a10",t:"l1",k:"mc",q:"The Mars Climate Orbiter was lost because:",o:["Units were not converted from imperial to metric", "A hacker stole the mission control passwords", "A rounding bug in the trading software", "The flight software was never tested at all"],a:0,e:"الوحدات ما تحولت من imperial إلى metric."},
{id:"a11",t:"l1",k:"mc",q:"Attributes of good software include:",o:["Maintainable, dependable, usable","Cheap, fast, colorful","Large, complex, closed","Written in one language"],a:0,e:"Maintainable و Dependable و Usable، مع تحقيق الـ FR و NFR."},
{id:"a12",t:"l1",k:"tf",q:"There is one best development method that suits all types of systems.",a:false,e:"يعتمد على نوع النظام. الألعاب بـ prototypes، والأنظمة الحرجة تبي توثيق دقيق."},

{id:"b1",t:"l2",m:["462", "461"],k:"mc",q:"The four software engineering activities in logical order are:",o:["Specification → Development → Verification &amp; validation → Evolution","Development → Specification → Evolution → Validation","Specification → Validation → Development → Evolution","Design → Coding → Testing → Management"],a:0,e:"سؤال متكرر بالميدات، والترتيب عليه درجات."},
{id:"b2",t:"l2",m:["451"],k:"mc",q:"The following is NOT a software engineering process activity:",o:["Software management","Software specification","Software design","Software evolution"],a:0,e:"ميد 451. Management مو من الأربع، والـ design داخل development."},
{id:"b3",t:"l2",k:"mc",q:"In which activity do we make sure the software is what the customer needs?",o:["Verification and validation", "Specification", "Evolution", "Design and implementation"],a:0,e:"V&amp;V."},
{id:"b4",t:"l2",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"One drawback of SaaS is:",o:["Security/trust vulnerabilities and internet dependence","Guaranteed performance","Full developer control","Free on-prem hardware"],a:0,e:"ميد 471."},
{id:"b5",t:"l2",k:"mc",q:"One benefit of SaaS is:",o:["Pay as you go","Full control","Works without internet","Unlimited range of applications"],a:0,e:"تدفع على قد استخدامك. والباقي عكس الصحيح."},
{id:"b6",t:"l2",k:"tf",q:"SaaS gives the user full control over the software.",a:false,e:"Lack of control من عيوبه."},
{id:"b7",t:"l2",k:"mc",q:"With web-based software, specifying all requirements in advance is no longer practical, so we use:",o:["Incremental development","Waterfall","Big-bang integration","No requirements at all"],a:0,e:"وصار الـ reuse مهم بعد."},
{id:"b8",t:"l2",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"\"Disclose to all concerned parties those conflicts of interest that cannot reasonably be avoided\" is:",o:["JUDGMENT","MANAGEMENT","PROFESSION","CLIENT AND EMPLOYER"],a:0,e:"conflicts of interest = JUDGMENT. جات في ميد 462."},
{id:"b9",t:"l2",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"\"Maintain the integrity of data, being sensitive to outdated or flawed occurrences\" is:",o:["PRODUCT","PROFESSION","PUBLIC","SELF"],a:0,e:"integrity of data = PRODUCT."},
{id:"b10",t:"l2",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"\"Give a fair hearing to the opinions, concerns, or complaints of a colleague\" is:",o:["COLLEAGUES","JUDGMENT","SELF","PUBLIC"],a:0,e:"كلمة colleague."},
{id:"b11",t:"l2",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"\"Ensure that software engineers are informed of standards before being held to them\" is:",o:["MANAGEMENT","PRODUCT","PROFESSION","COLLEAGUES"],a:0,e:"informed of standards = MANAGEMENT."},
{id:"b12",t:"l2",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"\"Accept full responsibility for their own work\" is:",o:["PUBLIC","SELF","PRODUCT","JUDGMENT"],a:0,e:"responsibility for their own work = PUBLIC."},
{id:"b13",t:"l2",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"\"Not give unfair treatment to anyone because of any irrelevant prejudices\" is:",o:["SELF","COLLEAGUES","PUBLIC","MANAGEMENT"],a:0,e:"prejudices = SELF."},
{id:"b14",t:"l2",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"\"Ensure an appropriate method is used for any project on which they work\" is:",o:["PRODUCT","MANAGEMENT","JUDGMENT","PROFESSION"],a:0,e:"appropriate method = PRODUCT."},
{id:"b15",t:"l2",k:"mc",q:"\"Keep private any confidential information\" is:",o:["CLIENT AND EMPLOYER","SELF","JUDGMENT","PUBLIC"],a:0,e:"confidential = CLIENT AND EMPLOYER."},
{id:"b16",t:"l2",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"\"Approve software only if they believe it is safe, meets specifications and passes appropriate tests\" is:",o:["PUBLIC","PRODUCT","MANAGEMENT","COLLEAGUES"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. سلامة الناس = PUBLIC."},
{id:"b17",t:"l2",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"\"Ensure proper and achievable goals and objectives for any project\" is:",o:["PRODUCT","MANAGEMENT","PUBLIC","SELF"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. أهداف المشروع نفسه = PRODUCT."},
{id:"b18",t:"l2",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"\"Improve their ability to produce accurate, informative, and well-written documentation\" is:",o:["SELF","PRODUCT","PROFESSION","COLLEAGUES"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. Improve their ability = SELF."},
{id:"b19",t:"l2",m:["451"],k:"mc",q:"\"Ensure a realistic estimation of cost and plan on all projects\" is:",o:["MANAGEMENT","PROFESSION","JUDGMENT","SELF"],a:0,e:"ميد 451. تقدير التكلفة والخطة شغل إدارة."},
{id:"b20",t:"l2",m:["451"],k:"mc",q:"\"Shouldn't illegally obtain a software application for any purpose\" (choose from Management, Profession, Judgment, Self):",o:["PROFESSION","MANAGEMENT","JUDGMENT","SELF"],a:0,e:"ميد 451. احترام القانون يحمي سمعة المهنة."},

{id:"c1",t:"l3",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"A key weakness of the Waterfall model in the slides is:",o:["Inflexible to changing requirements and late problem discovery","Low documentation","Iterative","Lack of any structure"],a:0,e:"ميد 471."},
{id:"c2",t:"l3",k:"tf",q:"The Waterfall model produces little documentation.",a:false,e:"العكس، توثيقه كامل (Complete set of documentation) وهذي من مميزاته."},
{id:"c3",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"Which model has the strength \"Receive early customer feedback\"?",o:["Incremental development","Waterfall","Reuse-oriented","V-model"],a:0,e:"العميل يشوف كل نسخة ويعلق عليها."},
{id:"c4",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"A weakness of incremental development is:",o:["It may lead to poorly structured software", "It produces too much documentation", "Customer feedback arrives too late", "It cannot accommodate any change"],a:0,e:"ومعها Reduced visibility and control."},
{id:"c5",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"Reuse-oriented development is also called:",o:["Component-based","Incremental","Agile","Plan-driven"],a:0,e:"Component-based."},
{id:"c6",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"Which model has the weakness \"Compromises made on requirements\"?",o:["Reuse-oriented","Waterfall","Incremental","Agile"],a:0,e:"نتنازل عن متطلبات عشان تناسب المكونات الجاهزة."},
{id:"c7",t:"l3",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"To cope with change, there are two approaches:",o:["Prototyping &amp; incremental delivery","Code-and-fix &amp; big-bang integration","Change prevention &amp; big-bang integration","Waterfall with extended design &amp; late verification"],a:0,e:"ميد 471."},
{id:"c8",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"System prototyping supports:",o:["Change avoidance only","Change tolerance only","Both avoidance and tolerance","Neither"],a:0,e:"Incremental delivery هو اللي يدعم الاثنين."},
{id:"c9",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"Designing the process so changes can be added at low cost is:",o:["Change tolerance","Change avoidance","Refactoring","Evolution"],a:0,e:"Avoidance: نتوقع التغيير قبل. Tolerance: نستوعبه بتكلفة قليلة."},
{id:"c10",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"Which type of error is the most expensive to fix?",o:["Requirement error","Coding error","Design error","Typing error"],a:0,e:"لأن النظام لازم ينعاد تصميمه."},
{id:"c11",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"The largest share of maintenance is:",o:["Functional addition (65%)","Fault repairs (17%)","Environmental adaptation (18%)","Testing"],a:0,e:"إضافة وظائف لأن السوق أو البزنس تغير."},
{id:"c12",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"Which testing stage uses real data from the customer?",o:["Acceptance testing","Component testing","System testing","Unit testing"],a:0,e:"آخر مرحلة: Component ثم System ثم Acceptance."},
{id:"c13",t:"l3",m:["451"],k:"mc",q:"One of the essential software design activities is:",o:["Architectural design","Requirements design","Test design","Market design"],a:0,e:"ميد 451. الأنشطة: architectural و interface و component و database design."},
{id:"c14",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"Software specification is also called:",o:["Requirement engineering","Implementation","Evolution","Integration"],a:0,e:"Requirement engineering."},
{id:"c15",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"In the V-model, the requirements specification produces the:",o:["Acceptance test plan","System integration test plan","Sub-system integration test plan","Unit test plan"],a:0,e:"System specification ← system integration test plan، و System design ← sub-system integration test plan."},
{id:"c16",t:"l3",k:"mc",q:"\"Defects cascade\" means:",o:["A change in one component causes a problem in another", "Errors appear only during the coding stage", "Testing is done only once at the very end", "Defects are fixed automatically by the compiler"],a:0,e:"عشان كذا الاختبار لازم يكون Iterative."},

{id:"d1",t:"l4",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"In XP, the practice of continuously improving the code is:",o:["Refactoring","Pair programming","Test automation","Continuous integration"],a:0,e:"ميد 462."},
{id:"d2",t:"l4",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"Which is a key principle of Extreme Programming (XP)?",o:["Continuous feedback","Long-term planning","Heavy documentation","Fixed requirements"],a:0,e:"ميد 462."},
{id:"d3",t:"l4",m:["451"],k:"mc",q:"In Scrum, the inputs of sprint planning include:",o:["Team capacity","Sprint goal","Sprint backlog","Burndown chart"],a:0,e:"ميد 451. Sprint goal و Sprint backlog مخرجات."},
{id:"d4",t:"l4",k:"mc",q:"Focus Factor equals:",o:["Sprint Velocity ÷ (people × hours per day)", "Sprint Velocity ÷ (people × working days)", "(people × hours per day) ÷ Sprint Velocity", "Sprint Velocity × people × hours per day"],a:0,e:"قسمة على (الأشخاص × الساعات)، مو على الأشخاص بس."},
{id:"d5",t:"l4",k:"mc",q:"The ideal range of the Focus Factor is:",o:["0.6 to 0.8","0.1 to 0.3","0.9 to 1.2","1 to 1.5"],a:0,e:"0.6 – 0.8."},
{id:"d6",t:"l4",k:"mc",q:"Effective team capacity equals:",o:["Focus Factor × (people × hours per day × working days)", "Focus Factor ÷ (people × hours per day × working days)", "Velocity × (people × hours per day × working days)", "Focus Factor × (people × working days)"],a:0,e:"والأسبوع 5 أيام عمل."},
{id:"d7",t:"l4",k:"mc",q:"5 people, 8 hours a day, velocity 30. The Focus Factor is:",o:["0.75","0.6","6","1.33"],a:0,e:"30 ÷ (5 × 8) = 30 ÷ 40 = 0.75. مثال السلايد."},
{id:"d8",t:"l4",k:"mc",q:"A 3-week sprint has how many working days?",o:["15","21","14","10"],a:0,e:"3 × 5 = 15. نشيل الويكند."},
{id:"d9",t:"l4",k:"mc",q:"A Scrum sprint cycle usually lasts:",o:["2 to 4 weeks","1 day","6 months","1 year"],a:0,e:"2 – 4 أسابيع."},
{id:"d10",t:"l4",k:"mc",q:"The three parts of a user story are:",o:["Who, What, Why","Who, When, Where","Input, Process, Output","Goal, Question, Metric"],a:0,e:"الدور، الوظيفة، والسبب."},
{id:"d11",t:"l4",k:"tf",q:"Many automated tests mean that testing is complete.",a:false,e:"المبرمج ممكن يختصر ويكتب اختبارات ناقصة."},
{id:"d12",t:"l4",k:"mc",q:"Integrating every finished task into the system once all tests pass is:",o:["Continuous integration","Refactoring","Small releases","Simple design"],a:0,e:"Continuous integration."},
{id:"d13",t:"l4",k:"mc",q:"Two programmers reviewing and tidying each other's code is:",o:["Pair programming","Refactoring","On-site customer","Test-first"],a:0,e:"Pair programming."},
{id:"d14",t:"l4",k:"mc",q:"Agile is most suitable for:",o:["Small and medium-sized products","Very large regulated systems","Systems with fixed requirements","Distributed outsourced teams"],a:0,e:"ويحتاج عميل ملتزم يشارك."},
{id:"d15",t:"l4",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"\"Emphasis on cost estimation before starting\" fits:",o:["Plan-driven","Agile"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. كل شي يتخطط ويتقدر قبل."},
{id:"d16",t:"l4",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"\"Continuous integration and testing\" fits:",o:["Agile","Plan-driven"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. من ممارسات XP."},
{id:"d17",t:"l4",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"\"Use of detailed risk management\" fits:",o:["Plan-driven","Agile"],a:0,e:"ميد 461."},
{id:"d18",t:"l4",k:"mc",q:"\"The system is subject to regulation\" fits:",o:["Plan-driven","Agile"],a:0,e:"الأنظمة والقوانين تبي توثيق."},
{id:"d19",t:"l4",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"A project must integrate COTS gateways and vendor SDKs. Choose:",o:["Component-based","Agile","Plan-driven"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. COTS و SDKs = مكونات جاهزة."},
{id:"d20",t:"l4",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"6 co-located developers, daily feedback, features reprioritized often, beta in weeks. Choose:",o:["Agile","Plan-driven","Component-based"],a:0,e:"ميد 471."},
{id:"d21",t:"l4",m:["451"],k:"mc",q:"The target system is intended for safety-critical operations. Choose:",o:["Waterfall","Agile","Component-based"],a:0,e:"ميد 451. يحتاج تحليل وتوثيق كامل قبل التنفيذ."},
{id:"d22",t:"l4",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"Banking reporting: requirements fixed by regulation, 30 people, sign-offs and audit trails. Choose:",o:["Plan-driven","Agile","Component-based"],a:0,e:"ميد 471."},
{id:"d23",t:"l4",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"Next sprint backlog is 30 points while the team's average velocity is 25. The plan is:",o:["Prudent","Feasible"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. الـ backlog أكبر شوي من المعدل."},

{id:"e1",t:"l5",m:["462", "461"],k:"mc",q:"What does product quality depend on?",o:["Development process","Developer skills","Project size","All of the above"],a:0,e:"ميد 462 و 461."},
{id:"e2",t:"l5",m:["462", "461"],k:"mc",q:"The process attribute that focuses on how easy it is to understand the process definition is:",o:["Understandability","Standardization","Visibility","Measurability"],a:0,e:"ميد 462 و 461."},
{id:"e3",t:"l5",m:["451"],k:"mc",q:"Product quality relies on process quality, people quality, cost/time and:",o:["Development technology","Fulfilment of clients' requirements","Short delivery window","Office location"],a:0,e:"ميد 451."},
{id:"e4",t:"l5",k:"mc",q:"\"Are the results of activities and the progress clear from the outside?\" is:",o:["Visibility","Understandability","Robustness","Acceptability"],a:0,e:"Visibility."},
{id:"e5",t:"l5",k:"mc",q:"\"Does the process keep going when unexpected problems appear?\" is:",o:["Robustness","Reliability","Rapidity","Supportability"],a:0,e:"Robustness. أما Reliability: يمنع الأخطاء في المنتج."},
{id:"e6",t:"l5",k:"mc",q:"\"Is the process supported by tools?\" is:",o:["Supportability","Acceptability","Maintainability","Measurability"],a:0,e:"Supportability."},
{id:"e7",t:"l5",k:"mc",q:"The process improvement cycle is:",o:["Measure → Analyze → Change","Change → Measure → Analyze","Analyze → Change → Measure","Plan → Do → Check"],a:0,e:"Measure ثم Analyze ثم Change."},
{id:"e8",t:"l5",k:"mc",q:"\"The number of attributes in a class\" is a:",o:["Predictor metric","Control metric","Process attribute","Standard"],a:0,e:"Predictor يتنبأ بخصائص البرنامج."},
{id:"e9",t:"l5",k:"mc",q:"\"Time to repair defects\" is a:",o:["Control metric","Predictor metric","Product standard","Risk"],a:0,e:"Control يدعم إدارة العملية."},
{id:"e10",t:"l5",k:"mc",q:"The GQM order is:",o:["Goal → Question → Metric","Metric → Question → Goal","Question → Goal → Metric","Goal → Metric → Question"],a:0,e:"Goal ثم Question ثم Metric."},
{id:"e11",t:"l5",k:"mc",q:"For small projects, quality depends mainly on:",o:["Developer skills and technologies used","The development process only","The project budget","ISO 9001"],a:0,e:"الكبيرة تعتمد على الـ development process."},
{id:"e12",t:"l5",k:"tf",q:"Process improvement is driven by measurements.",a:false,e:"القياسات للتحليل بس، والتحسين يقوده الـ objectives."},
{id:"e13",t:"l5",k:"mc",q:"The two challenges of process change are:",o:["Resistance to change and change persistence", "Cost of new tools and training time", "Lack of standards and poor documentation", "Late testing and difficult integration"],a:0,e:"Resistance و Change persistence."},
{id:"e14",t:"l5",k:"mc",q:"A process supported by a specific development method such as RUP is:",o:["Methodical","Informal","Managed","Improving"],a:0,e:"Methodical."},
{id:"e15",t:"l5",k:"mc",q:"Documentation and coding standards are:",o:["Product standards","Process standards","Business standards","Risk standards"],a:0,e:"Process standards عن طريقة الشغل."},

{id:"f1",t:"l6",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"The project schedule chart includes:",o:["All of them","Tasks","People involved for each task","Milestones"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. المهام والناس والـ milestones."},
{id:"f2",t:"l6",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"The four factors of people management are:",o:["Consistency, Respect, Inclusion, Honesty","Consistency, Respect, Loyalty, Honesty","Consistency, Respect, Speed, Experience","Consistency, Experience, Inclusion, Honesty"],a:0,e:"ميد 461."},
{id:"f3",t:"l6",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"Risk management involves anticipating risks that may affect:",o:["The project schedule and the quality","The project schedule only","The quality only","None of them"],a:0,e:"ميد 461."},
{id:"f4",t:"l6",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"Which is NOT considered a risk in project management?",o:["Testing","Specification delays","Product competition","Hardware delays"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. Testing نشاط، مو خطر."},
{id:"f5",t:"l6",k:"mc",q:"Algorithmic cost modeling uses:",o:["Effort = A × Size^B × M","Effort = Size ÷ people","Effort = A + B + M","Effort = Velocity × days"],a:0,e:"Effort = A × Size^B × M."},
{id:"f6",t:"l6",k:"mc",q:"In Effort = A × Size^B × M, B is between:",o:["1 and 1.5","0 and 1","2 and 3","0.6 and 0.8"],a:0,e:"B بين 1 و 1.5."},
{id:"f7",t:"l6",m:["451"],k:"tf",q:"The initial estimation of engineers' effort is always accurate.",a:false,e:"ميد 451. لو التقدير x، الحقيقي بين 0.25x و 4x."},
{id:"f8",t:"l6",k:"tf",q:"Adding people to a late project makes it finish earlier.",a:false,e:"يخليه يتأخر أكثر."},
{id:"f9",t:"l6",k:"mc",q:"\"A competing product reaches the market before we finish\" is a:",o:["Business risk","Project risk","Product risk","Technical risk"],a:0,e:"Business يأثر على المنظمة نفسها."},
{id:"f10",t:"l6",k:"mc",q:"\"Essential hardware does not arrive on time\" is a:",o:["Project risk","Product risk","Business risk","People risk"],a:0,e:"Project يأثر على الجدول أو الموارد."},
{id:"f11",t:"l6",k:"mc",q:"\"The size of the system was underestimated\" is a:",o:["Product risk","Project risk","Business risk","Market risk"],a:0,e:"Product يأثر على جودة أو أداء المنتج."},
{id:"f12",t:"l6",k:"mc",q:"The risk management steps in order are:",o:["Identification → Analysis → Planning → Monitoring","Analysis → Identification → Monitoring → Planning","Planning → Identification → Analysis → Monitoring","Monitoring → Planning → Analysis → Identification"],a:0,e:"Identification ثم Analysis ثم Planning ثم Monitoring."},
{id:"f13",t:"l6",k:"mc",q:"A status meeting usually lasts:",o:["10 to 15 minutes", "45 to 60 minutes", "2 to 3 hours", "A full working day"],a:0,e:"قصير، ومرة بالأسبوع على الأقل."},
{id:"f14",t:"l6",k:"mc",q:"In a brainstorming session:",o:["No idea is criticized during the session", "Each idea is evaluated as soon as it is said", "Only senior members are allowed to suggest ideas", "The team agrees on one idea before starting"],a:0,e:"التقييم يكون في الآخر، مو وقت الجلسة."},
{id:"f15",t:"l6",k:"mc",q:"Small teams are better because:",o:["They have fewer communication problems", "They can skip the testing phase safely", "They do not need a project manager", "They always finish faster than big teams"],a:0,e:"أقل من 10، ومشاكل التواصل أقل والفريق متماسك."},
{id:"f16",t:"l6",k:"mc",q:"If requirements are likely to change, the company may:",o:["Offer a low price, then charge for changes", "Freeze the requirements for the whole project", "Double the price before any work starts", "Refuse to sign any contract with the client"],a:0,e:"Requirements volatility: سعر أقل أول، وبعدين يحاسب على التغييرات."},

{id:"g1",t:"l7",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"\"The system should be easy to use for first-year students.\"",o:["User · NFR","System · FR","User · FR","System · NFR"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. جملة عامة، و easy to use جودة."},
{id:"g2",t:"l7",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"\"The application shall allow password reset using a verified email.\"",o:["System · FR","User · NFR","User · FR","System · NFR"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. خدمة محددة بتفاصيلها."},
{id:"g3",t:"l7",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"\"The interface will display student GPA to two decimal places.\"",o:["System · FR","User · FR","User · NFR","System · NFR"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. تفصيل دقيق، وهي خدمة عرض."},
{id:"g4",t:"l7",m:["471"],k:"tf",q:"\"The report generation shall be fast.\" is a functional requirement because it uses \"shall\".",a:false,e:"ميد 471. fast جودة، فهي NFR. كلمة shall ما تحدد النوع."},
{id:"g5",t:"l7",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"\"All new services must be built in Java 21 and deployed on the organization's Kubernetes platform.\"",o:["Organization","Product","External"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. لغة أو منصة تفرضها الشركة."},
{id:"g6",t:"l7",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"\"Patient data must comply with HIPAA and local privacy law X.\"",o:["External","Organization","Product"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. قانون = External."},
{id:"g7",t:"l7",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"\"The API shall respond in ≤ 300 ms for read requests under 100 concurrent users.\"",o:["Product","Organization","External"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. أداء المنتج نفسه."},
{id:"g8",t:"l7",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"\"Device firmware must interoperate with ISO/IEC 14443 Type A NFC readers.\"",o:["External","Product","Organization"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. معيار خارجي."},
{id:"g9",t:"l7",k:"mc",q:"In requirements, \"shall\" means:",o:["Mandatory","Desirable","Optional","Deprecated"],a:0,e:"shall إلزامي، و should مرغوب."},
{id:"g10",t:"l7",k:"mc",q:"The most widely used way to write requirements is:",o:["Structured natural language","Mathematical specification","Design description language","Graphical notations"],a:0,e:"Structured natural language."},
{id:"g11",t:"l7",k:"mc",q:"Finding the other requirements affected by a change is:",o:["Traceability management","Requirement storage","Change management","Validation"],a:0,e:"Traceability management."},
{id:"g12",t:"l7",k:"mc",q:"Reliability is measured by:",o:["Mean time to failure","Training time","Megabytes","Number of systems it runs on"],a:0,e:"Ease of use بـ training time، و Portability بعدد الأنظمة."},
{id:"g13",t:"l7",k:"mc",q:"User requirements are:",o:["High-level, in plain language","Detailed and precise","Written in code","Only for developers"],a:0,e:"System requirements هي المفصلة."},
{id:"g14",t:"l7",k:"tf",q:"A non-functional requirement can be more important than a functional one.",a:true,e:"بدونه ممكن النظام ما يشتغل أصلاً."},
{id:"g15",t:"l7",k:"mc",q:"\"Patient information should be end-to-end encrypted.\"",o:["NFR · Product","FR","NFR · External","NFR · Organization"],a:0,e:"مثال السلايد."},

{id:"h1",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"The requirements engineering process is:",o:["Elicitation → Analysis &amp; specification → Validation","Design → Coding → Testing","Validation → Elicitation → Specification","Analysis → Design → Evolution"],a:0,e:"ثلاث مراحل."},
{id:"h2",t:"l8",k:"tf",q:"If the answer to any of the feasibility study questions is no, we probably should not go ahead with the project.",a:true,e:"Feasibility study قصيرة وتكون بدري."},
{id:"h3",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"Which is NOT a feasibility study question?",o:["Which programming language is the fastest?","Does the system contribute to the organization's objectives?","Can it be implemented within schedule and budget?","Can it be integrated with other systems?"],a:0,e:"الثلاث الثانية هي الأسئلة."},
{id:"h4",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"The four stages of elicitation and analysis start with:",o:["Requirement discovery","Requirements specification","Prioritization and negotiation","Validation"],a:0,e:"Discovery ثم Classification ثم Prioritization ثم Specification."},
{id:"h5",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"Finding and resolving conflicts between stakeholders happens in:",o:["Requirements prioritization and negotiation","Requirement discovery","Classification and organisation","Feasibility study"],a:0,e:"Prioritization and negotiation."},
{id:"h6",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"Which is NOT a requirements discovery technique?",o:["Refactoring","Interviewing","Scenarios","Ethnography"],a:0,e:"الأربع: interviews و scenarios و use cases و ethnography."},
{id:"h7",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"An interview where the stakeholder answers predefined questions is:",o:["Closed interview","Open interview","Ethnography","Scenario"],a:0,e:"Open: ما فيه أسئلة محددة."},
{id:"h8",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"The analyst gets deeply into the working environment to reveal implicit requirements. This is:",o:["Ethnography","Interviewing","Use case","Prototyping"],a:0,e:"Ethnography: دراسة السياق الاجتماعي والتنظيمي."},
{id:"h9",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"A use case is mainly used to capture:",o:["Functional requirements","Non-functional requirements","Hardware costs","Project risks"],a:0,e:"ويحدد الـ actors، ويوثق بـ UML."},
{id:"h10",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"A real-life example of how to interact with the system, with normal flow and what may go wrong, is a:",o:["Scenario","Use case diagram","Feasibility study","Prototype"],a:0,e:"Scenario."},
{id:"h11",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"A reason elicitation is difficult:",o:["Stakeholders often don't know what they want","Stakeholders always agree","Requirements never change","There is only one stakeholder"],a:0,e:"ومن الأسباب بعد: political factors وتغير بيئة البزنس."},
{id:"h12",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"Ensuring requirements can actually be implemented is:",o:["Realism","Validity","Consistency","Completeness"],a:0,e:"Realism."},
{id:"h13",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"Making sure there are no missing requirements is:",o:["Completeness","Consistency","Realism","Verifiability"],a:0,e:"Completeness."},
{id:"h14",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"Resolving conflicting requirements is:",o:["Consistency","Completeness","Validity","Realism"],a:0,e:"Consistency."},
{id:"h15",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"Writing requirements so that a set of tests can be written for them is:",o:["Verifiability","Validity","Realism","Completeness"],a:0,e:"Verifiability."},
{id:"h16",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"Which is a requirements validation technique?",o:["Test-case generation","Ethnography","Refactoring","Pair programming"],a:0,e:"الثلاث: reviews و prototyping و test-case generation."},
{id:"h17",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"An effective interviewer should be:",o:["Open-minded, avoiding preconceived ideas","Strict with predefined answers only","Silent","Focused on the code"],a:0,e:"ومستعد يسمع ويحرك النقاش."},
{id:"h18",t:"l8",k:"mc",q:"Requirements validation means:",o:["Checking requirements define the system the customer really wants", "Estimating how much the system will cost to build", "Writing the code that implements each requirement", "Deploying the system to the customer's servers"],a:0,e:"نتأكد إن المتطلبات هي اللي يبيها العميل فعلاً."},
{id:"m1",t:"l6",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Which of the following is one of the main duties of a software project manager?",o:["Writing source code for every module personally", "Estimating costs, scheduling tasks, and monitoring project development", "Performing all unit testing on behalf of the team", "Making all technical design decisions without team input"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. التقدير والجدولة والمتابعة من مهام المدير."},
{id:"m2",t:"l6",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"A successful software project should:",o:["Deliver all planned features regardless of the deadline or cost", "Be delivered on time, within budget, and meet the agreed requirements", "Minimize cost above every other criterion", "Maximize the number of customer meetings during development"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. في الوقت، وضمن الميزانية، ويحقق المتطلبات."},
{id:"m3",t:"l6",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Which item is normally included in a project plan?",o:["Sample source code for each task", "Risk analysis, resource requirements, and a work breakdown", "A list of developer salaries", "The product's marketing strategy"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. الـ plan فيه المخاطر والموارد وتقسيم العمل."},
{id:"m4",t:"l6",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Why should project tasks be self-contained where possible?",o:["They are harder to test in isolation", "They increase coupling between tasks", "They are easier to estimate, manage, and test independently", "They force a fixed order of development"],a:2,e:"ميد 472. المهمة المستقلة أسهل في التقدير والإدارة والاختبار."},
{id:"m5",t:"l6",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Which of the following best qualifies as a project milestone?",o:["Fixing a single syntax error in a module", "Completion and formal sign-off of the requirements specification", "Installing a web browser on the developer's machine", "Adding a comment to the project wiki"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. الـ milestone نقطة مهمة لها مخرج رسمي."},
{id:"m6",t:"l6",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"What is the main purpose of risk management in software project management?",o:["To replace the need for detailed planning", "To identify risks, assess their impact, and plan responses before problems occur", "To increase the project budget automatically", "To substitute for the testing phase"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. نحدد المخاطر ونقيّمها ونخطط لها قبل ما تصير."},
{id:"m7",t:"l6",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Which of the following is part of people management?",o:["Selecting team members and assigning suitable roles", "Removing stakeholder requirements to save effort", "Replacing the project schedule with source code", "Cancelling performance reviews to build trust"],a:0,e:"ميد 472. اختيار الفريق وتوزيع الأدوار."},
{id:"m8",t:"l3",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"A safety-critical avionics control system with strict regulatory certification and well-defined, rarely changing requirements. Which process model is most appropriate?",o:["Scrum with two-week sprints and no formal documentation", "A plan-driven (waterfall / V-model) process with full documentation and formal reviews at each stage", "Ad-hoc coding without a defined process", "Big-bang integration at the very end of development"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. safety-critical ومتطلبات ثابتة، فيناسبه Plan-driven."},
{id:"m9",t:"l6",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Why should task dependencies be minimized in project planning?",o:["To reduce the need for project monitoring", "To enable parallel work and limit the impact of task delays", "To eliminate the need for documentation", "To reduce communication between team members"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. يسمح بالشغل المتوازي ويقلل أثر التأخير."},
{id:"m10",t:"l6",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Which set of activities is the most appropriate for project planning?",o:["Writing source code, debugging modules, and deploying the final system", "Setting milestones, breaking work into tasks, estimating time and resources, and minimizing task dependencies", "Drawing only UML diagrams and ignoring scheduling constraints", "Focusing only on team motivation without defining deliverables"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. هذي أنشطة الـ Project planning."},
{id:"m11",t:"l7",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"A functional requirement is best described as:",o:["A constraint on project cost only", "A service or behavior that the system must provide", "The choice of programming language used in the project", "A project milestone or deadline"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. الـ FR خدمة أو سلوك يقدمه النظام."},
{id:"m12",t:"l7",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Which of the following is a non-functional requirement?",o:["The system shall allow students to reset their passwords", "The system shall generate a transcript as a PDF document", "The system shall respond to any search request in less than 2 seconds", "The system shall allow advisors to approve registration requests"],a:2,e:"ميد 472. زمن الاستجابة صفة أداء، فهو NFR."},
{id:"m13",t:"l7",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"User requirements are usually:",o:["Expressed only as source code", "High-level statements understandable by non-technical stakeholders", "More detailed than system requirements", "Written only by developers for developers"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. عامة ومفهومة لغير التقنيين."},
{id:"m14",t:"l7",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Which statement is the best example of an ambiguous requirement?",o:["The system shall store each student's ID, name, and email", "The system shall be user-friendly and fast", "The system shall lock an account after three failed login attempts", "The system shall export reports in PDF format"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. «user-friendly and fast» ما تنقاس."},
{id:"m15",t:"l8",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"In requirements engineering, validation mainly checks whether the requirements are:",o:["Syntactically well-formatted in a single language", "Valid, consistent, complete, realistic, and verifiable", "Implemented in an object-oriented language", "Partitioned into independent modules"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. الفحوصات الخمسة."},
{id:"m16",t:"l4",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Which process model is most suitable when requirements change frequently and customer feedback is continuous?",o:["Waterfall", "Agile", "Pure plan-driven", "Big-bang integration"],a:1,e:"ميد 472. تغيير مستمر و feedback مستمر."},
{id:"m17",t:"l7",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"\"The system should be easy for new students to learn within one lab session.\"",o:["User · NFR", "User · FR", "System · FR", "System · NFR"],a:0,e:"ميد 472. جملة عامة عن سهولة التعلم."},
{id:"m18",t:"l7",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"\"The system shall allow an instructor to upload course files in PDF format.\"",o:["System · FR", "User · NFR", "System · NFR", "User · FR"],a:0,e:"ميد 472. خدمة (upload) مع تفصيل تقني (PDF)."},
{id:"m19",t:"l7",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"\"The application shall support at least 500 concurrent users during registration.\"",o:["System · NFR", "System · FR", "User · FR", "User · NFR"],a:0,e:"ميد 472. رقم ينقاس عن الأداء."},
{id:"m20",t:"l7",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"\"The system shall encrypt all stored passwords using the SHA-256 algorithm.\"",o:["System · NFR", "System · FR", "User · FR", "User · NFR"],a:0,e:"ميد 472. خوارزمية محددة عن الأمان. كلمة shall ما تخليها FR."},
{id:"m21",t:"l3",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Five developers, weekly customer feedback, features re-prioritized frequently, an early working version needed quickly. Which model?",o:["Agile", "Plan-Driven", "Component-Based", "Waterfall"],a:0,e:"ميد 472. feedback أسبوعي وتغيير كثير ونسخة سريعة."},
{id:"m22",t:"l4",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Last four sprints: 18, 22, 20 and 24 story points. The average sprint velocity is:",o:["21", "20", "22", "84"],a:0,e:"ميد 472. المجموع 84، و 84 ÷ 4 = 21."},
{id:"m23",t:"l6",m:["472"],k:"mc",q:"Tasks of 5, 8, 4 and 7 days. Task 3 runs in parallel with Task 2; Tasks 1 and 4 stay sequential. Total duration?",o:["20 days", "24 days", "16 days", "19 days"],a:0,e:"ميد 472. ناخذ الأطول من 8 و 4، فيصير 5 + 8 + 7 = 20."},
{id:"x1",t:"l7",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"\"The report generation shall be fast.\"",o:["User · NFR", "User · FR", "System · FR", "System · NFR"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. fast صفة جودة، فهي NFR. وعامة بدون رقم، فهي User."},
{id:"x2",t:"l4",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"Last 4 sprints completed 22, 28, 26 and 24 story points. The sprint velocity (average) is:",o:["25", "24", "26", "100"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. المجموع 100، و 100 ÷ 4 = 25."},
{id:"x3",t:"l3",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"Medical device companion app: must follow IEC 62304 and ISO 14971, uses a certified vendor SDK, 15 people. Choose:",o:["Plan-Driven", "Agile", "Component-Based"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. فيه SDK، بس الـ compliance أقوى ويحتاج توثيق كامل."},
{id:"x4",t:"l7",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"\"The mobile app shall support offline read-only access for 24 hours.\"",o:["Product", "Organization", "External"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. سلوك المنتج وقت التشغيل."},
{id:"x5",t:"l7",m:["471"],k:"mc",q:"\"The system shall export reports in CSV and PDF.\"",o:["Product", "Organization", "External"],a:0,e:"ميد 471. يخص المنتج نفسه."},
{id:"x6",t:"l7",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"Task Management System: employees create tasks, assign them and update their status; the system handles 100 concurrent users and encrypts data. Which is a functional requirement?",o:["Employees can update the status of their tasks", "The system handles 100 concurrent users without delays", "User data is encrypted during transmission", "Pages respond to users without noticeable delays"],a:0,e:"ميد 462. تحديث الحالة خدمة يقدمها النظام."},
{id:"x7",t:"l7",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"Task Management System: employees create tasks, assign them and update their status; the system handles 100 concurrent users and encrypts data. Which is a non-functional requirement?",o:["User data is encrypted during transmission", "Employees can create tasks with a due date", "Employees can assign tasks to team members", "Employees can update the status of their tasks"],a:0,e:"ميد 462. التشفير صفة أمان، فهو NFR."},
{id:"x8",t:"l3",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"Project 1: stakeholders give initial requirements only, requirements stable, large multi-team project, distributed teams communicating through documentation. Choose:",o:["Plan-Driven", "Iterative", "Agile"],a:0,e:"ميد 462. متطلبات ثابتة وفريق كبير وموزع ويعتمد على التوثيق."},
{id:"x9",t:"l3",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"Project 2: stakeholders highly involved, requirements change often, 5 co-located developers with daily stand-ups. Choose:",o:["Plan-Driven", "Iterative", "Agile"],a:2,e:"ميد 462. تغيير كثير و feedback مستمر وفريق صغير."},
{id:"x10",t:"l3",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"Project 3: periodic reviews, moderate change with a stable core, 15 co-located developers, regular iterations to refine the product. Choose:",o:["Plan-Driven", "Iterative", "Agile"],a:1,e:"ميد 462. كل شي متوسط، والنص يقول regular iterations."},
{id:"x11",t:"l3",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"Project 4: reviews only at milestones, stable documented requirements, focus on regulatory compliance, structured process. Choose:",o:["Plan-Driven", "Iterative", "Agile"],a:0,e:"ميد 462. متطلبات ثابتة و compliance يحتاج توثيق."},
{id:"x12",t:"l3",m:["451"],k:"mc",q:"The clients need to see prototypes of the developed system and give early feedback. Choose:",o:["Agile", "Waterfall", "Component-based"],a:0,e:"ميد 451. العميل يشوف نسخ صغيرة متتالية ويعلق عليها."},
{id:"x13",t:"l2",m:["451"],k:"mc",q:"Which is an example of adhering to the PUBLIC principle?",o:["Approve software only if it is safe and passes appropriate tests", "Improve their knowledge of the Code and how to apply it", "Assist colleagues in learning current standard work practices", "Ensure a realistic estimation of cost and plan on projects"],a:0,e:"ميد 451. السلامة مصلحة عامة، فهي PUBLIC."},
{id:"x14",t:"l2",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"\"Assist colleagues in being fully aware of current standard work practices\" is:",o:["COLLEAGUES", "SELF", "MANAGEMENT", "PROFESSION"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. كلمة colleagues."},
{id:"x15",t:"l4",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"\"Flexibility in handling changing requirements\" fits:",o:["Agile", "Plan-driven"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. Agile مبني على قبول التغيير."},
{id:"x16",t:"l4",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"\"Incremental delivery of features\" fits:",o:["Agile", "Plan-driven"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. التسليم على دفعات صغيرة."},
{id:"x17",t:"l4",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"\"Long periods of planning and analysis\" fits:",o:["Plan-driven", "Agile"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. تخطيط طويل قبل التنفيذ."},
{id:"x18",t:"l7",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"Equipment hire system: bookings, customer records, returns, a daily summary; each page must load within 5 seconds. Which is a non-functional requirement?",o:["Each page must load within 5 seconds", "Record the return of an item after the hire", "Check whether the customer hired equipment before", "Make an advance booking for an available item"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. زمن التحميل صفة أداء."},
{id:"x19",t:"l7",m:["461"],k:"mc",q:"Equipment hire system: bookings, customer records, returns, a daily summary; each page must load within 5 seconds. Which is a functional requirement?",o:["Record the return of an item after the hire", "Each page must load within 5 seconds", "The system is available during working hours", "The minimum period of hire is one day"],a:0,e:"ميد 461. تسجيل الإرجاع خدمة يقدمها النظام."},
{id:"x20",t:"l2",m:["462"],k:"mc",q:"\"Improve their knowledge of this Code, its interpretation, and its application to their work\" is:",o:["SELF","PROFESSION","MANAGEMENT","COLLEAGUES"],a:0,e:"ميد 462. improve their knowledge = SELF."}
]};
